{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533133-the-promise-of-1528","id":1533133,"title":"The Promise of 1528","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-03-25T13:43:59-07:00","id":1533133,"title":"The Promise of 1528","content":"Cult of the Blood Gods has a lore sheet for the promise of 1528 between the Giovanni and the Cam. With it coming due in less than four years it seems ripe for an entire campaign.<br /> <br /> It indicates that both sides are currently scrambling to figure out the details of the agreement so they can deal with the consequences.<br /> <br /> Where might players search to find the details of the promise? What promises would create interesting plotlines?<br /> Are the rest of the Hecata going to play ball with a promise made by only a subset?<br /> Will the Cam try to wrest Venice from the Hecata?<br /> <br /> Help me brainstorm ideas!<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-25T17:52:14-07:00","id":1533143,"title":"","content":"Were I storytelling, I'd put forth all kinds of omens, portents, and speculations on the nature of the Promise by occult scholars, only to have it turn out that it was just what it seemed to be, a 500-year peace treaty that the Giovanni brokered to buy themselves enough time to consolidate power as a clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-25T20:38:18-07:00","id":1533151,"title":"","content":"We've never gotten an exact write-up of the Promise, but in general it seems that the Giovanni promised to stay independent and out of both the Camarilla and the Sabbat's affairs and respect the Camarilla's power, and in exchange the Camarilla essentially agreed to leave them alone and wouldn't intervene when they killed Cappadocians in Camarilla cities. The Camarilla basically washed their hands of the Cappadocian/Giovanni civil war allowed the Giovanni to do what they wanted, as long as they didn't join the Sabbat (which was likely trying to recruit these guys since they'd killed their Clan founder and were a poster-child for the Sabbat's goals), and agreed to respect the Camarilla's traditions and certain territorial and Embracing rules.<br /> <br /> In V20, with the Promise ending, the Giovanni would be in a good place to join the Camarilla. By this point in time they've essentially &quot;won&quot; and beaten the Cappadocians, and with the Gangrel leaving they could get a lot of power in the Camarilla by joining. So Agustus would probably be considering that sort of move and it wouldn't be a complete shock if the Promise ended and the Giovanni officially moved into the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> In W5 though, the idea of the Giovanni (now Hecata) joining is pretty unlikely. After losing the Brujah, the Camarilla would love to have them even more than in V20, but now the Hecata are controlled by a lot of Cappadocians, many of whom probably hold a bit of a grudge against the Camarilla for agreeing to &quot;sell them out&quot; to the Giovanni. Plus, many members are on Paths and quite a few Harbringers likely still have allies among the Sabbat. As such the Hecata would be far more likely to remain independent.<br /> <br /> In W5, I think it's unlikely that you would see the Camarilla move against Venice after what happened there. The Tremere would probably be gung-ho to snatch the Giovanni's secrets, but they're in no position to try something like that. The other clans wouldn't likely have much interest in the Giovanni's occult lore. The Venture might be interested in getting some of their finances, but I suspect they would probably try to pressure the Hecata/Giovanni financially rather than do something like try to physically take over Venice.<br /> <br /> If anything, I suspect you would see a concentrated effort by the Anarchs to try and recruit the Hecata, and you might see the Sabbat remnants trying to move into Venice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 03-25-2024, 11:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T12:13:41-07:00","id":1533184,"title":"","content":"The Hecate joining the Anarchs would be a scary thought for the Camarilla sect leadership.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T16:39:09-07:00","id":1533216,"title":"","content":"This entire question is a good example why we are now dealing with multiple versions of the setting as the canon has changed considerably from edition to edition.<br /> <br /> When the Giovanni were introduced, there was no mention of the Promise of 1528. But something very much like it was stated. All we knew is that the other vampires were hunting down and destroying the Giovanni (the Devil Kindred) for slaying their founder and its other descendants. To stop their own destruction, the Giovanni pledged to maintain a low profile and keep out of Kindred politics. It was also mentioned that Augustus Giovanni limited only 3 members every generation to be embraced (if we assume that is one very decade, then only around 50 Giovanni had been embrace since the year 1500 meaning the clan is incredibly small). While not explicitly part of the earlier agreement, I always assumed this was in fact a condition of the Giovanni making peace with the Camarilla to prevent their own destruction. From the clan description, we know the Giovanni are extremely wealthy and have some amount of power, but also seem very vulnerable because of their lower numbers and general contempt for them by other vampires. Like the Assamites with the Treaty of Tyre, we have the impression that while the Giovanni are not included in the Inner Circle they are pretty much part of the Camarilla system with internal autonomy among their clan, but pretty much regulated by the Inner Circle in terms of how they deal with other vampires.<br /> <br /> The idea of limiting how many Giovanni were embraced was quickly forgotten. And in the Giovanni clanbook, we're finally given a name to the peace agreement - the Promise of 1528. It also for the first time ties together the Giovanni being from Venice with why the Camarilla meets in Venice. While there is some nice flavor text finally being given to the backstory, the clanbook unfortunately begins turning the Giovanni into something they weren't before. Instead of being see as the modern equivalent of the Borgia family, a corrupt family of Renaissance Italian merchant princes, and simultaneously powerful and weak among the vampires, they are now a bunch of goomba southern Italian mobsters whose numbers and power approach those of the other clans, and they really aren't limited all that much by the Promise. The Giovanni were pretty much de facto independent with little oversight and do whatever they like.<br /> <br /> In Revised this gets worse with the clan assuming even more power and numbers, and because the world was ending, they were very far along the way of completing whatever metaplot function they served by helping to usher in doomsday while the Camarilla looks upon things helplessly.<br /> <br /> V20 set back things to the old 2e standard, but still had the Giovanni be far bigger and more independent than it was implied they were in 1e.<br /> <br /> I am assuming V5 is where we're told there is now a 500 year time limit to the Promise of 1528. I don't think that existed before. So it's a new setting. Although why there'd be a time limit does not seem to have been provided. Nor do we seem to be told what exactly this means in terms what they could or could not do before since the idea that Giovanni are forbidden to involve themselves in Kindred affairs has never been developed, as every time I've seen Giovanni played that seems to be all they do. Presumably this means they could now join the Sabbat or some other enemy sect. But if so, why the hell would the Camarilla ever allow that? Personally the only reason it would make sense to me for any kind of 500 year term would be something like, &quot;We will be giving you a 500 year probationary period. If you behave yourselves and perform well, we will consider your clan's application to join us on the Inner Circle.&quot; Otherwise what is the point? Why surrender whatever authority you had? What could the Giovanni have given the Camarilla to simply give them this out?<br /> <br /> It doesn't make sense as an IC setting element. It only makes since as an OOC derived element the writers threw in their in order to make things more &quot;exciting&quot;. The very idea that both sides are &quot;scrambling&quot; to figure the details out is absurd. If it actually existed, then both sides would ALREADY have known the details for 500 years, and have been filling in any gaps for all this time every 13 years cycle when the Inner Circle checks up on the Giovanni. To me, this is all fake drama and not well thought out by the writers.<br /> <br /> Of course with the V5 scenario of Augustus killed, the Giovanni family overthrown, and re-establishment of the Cappadocian clan (although now called the Hecata), I'm not exactly sure what relevance of the Promise of 1528 has anymore. Most members of the Hecata have never been ruled by it except insofar the Camarilla allowed Augustus to do what he wanted with the other Cappadocians since they were now of &quot;his&quot; blood. For we never saw anyone ever argue that the Samedi or other surviving Cappadocians had to abide by the Promise. Once the Family Reunion happened, the thing that makes the most sense is that when the Inner Circle next convenes they would figure out what they wanted to do about the Hecata - and the most likely scenario would be for them to offer them membership on the Inner Circle and establish a new Justicar for the new clan. And they wouldn't need any 500 year clause in their agreement with the Giovanni to do that.<br /> <br /> But I'm of the opinion that almost the entirety of the Revised/V5 metaplot has been detrimental to the setting and created this bizarre Earth-2 (or is it Earth-3 by now) version of the World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-27T06:11:47-07:00","id":1533247,"title":"","content":"At that point I believe that the V5 will just ignore the promise or treat it as a non-aggression contract that is in their interest to keep, after all I think it should be out of focus by now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-27T08:26:58-07:00","id":1533253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533133-the-promise-of-1528?p=1533247#post1533247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At that point I believe that the V5 will just ignore the promise or treat it as a non-aggression contract that is in their interest to keep, after all I think it should be out of focus by now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually this makes me think that the promise could be a center plot piece in a sixth edition. Four years is probably enough time that sixth edition is very likely.<br /> <br /> I really ask this question more as I am contemplating a Venice by night campaign and making tidbits of 1528 a centerpiece of my campaign. Old elders to track down to get information from. Possible political shifts being negotiated etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-27T21:07:21-07:00","id":1533295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RadioFreeDeath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533133-the-promise-of-1528?p=1533253#post1533253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually this makes me think that the promise could be a center plot piece in a sixth edition. Four years is probably enough time that sixth edition is very likely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to be a debbie downer, but I doubt that. The Promise has become largely irrelevant in 5th edition. The Giovanni functionally no longer exist. Most of the elders who would have signed the Promise are dead, and the survivors of the clan have been subsumed into the Hecata. And the majority of the Hecata (Cappadocians, Harbringers, Samedi and Nagaraja) were never bound by the Promise to begin with. So when the Promise ends, it won't have much of a change on the Hecata, unless the clan ends up joining the Camarilla or the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> If anything I would expect there to be a moment where the Camarilla says, &quot;The Promise is ending next year,&quot; and the Hecata go, &quot;Huh? Oh, that? Yeah, well we ain't the guys who signed the Promise with you, and the ones who did are all dead, so it's not really our business.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-27T22:14:31-07:00","id":1533299,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m looking right at my original Clanbook: Giovanni (1997) and it mentions the Promise of 1528. It doesn\u2019t mention a 500 year expiration date, though the idea seems cool to me. Waiting 30 years in real life for the 500 year old in game deadline seems awesome, especially if something important happens.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, V5 basically made significant future events tied to the Giovanni highly unlikely I\u2019m not impossible.<br /> <br /> If it were up to me, I might have this be a major metaplot event, with the Giovanni being courted by various factions now that they can get involved more directly in Kindred politics. Joining the Camarilla seems like a natural choice to me, especially with Harbringers in the Sabbat.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-28T10:22:56-07:00","id":1533319,"title":"","content":"Could make for an interesting setting but would be version dependent. <br /> <br /> Giovanni joining the Cam? I'm thinking the Venture would roll them into submission. Giovanni may have ghosts, but Ventrue have a lot more. <br /> <br /> Hecata joining the Anarchs? Not sure that makes sense. Clan of ancient necromancers is gonna help youngsters fight the elders? I could see them helping both sides against the middle to make more dead people but would they even care? <br /> <br /> V5, IMO, they stay kinda independent like the Nosferatu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-28T20:05:40-07:00","id":1533346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RadioFreeDeath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533133-the-promise-of-1528?p=1533253#post1533253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually this makes me think that the promise could be a center plot piece in a sixth edition. Four years is probably enough time that sixth edition is very likely.<br /> <br /> I really ask this question more as I am contemplating a Venice by night campaign and making tidbits of 1528 a centerpiece of my campaign. Old elders to track down to get information from. Possible political shifts being negotiated etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why will they release a sixth edition? Is there anything in the corebook they want to change?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-30T15:48:16-07:00","id":1533396,"title":"","content":"I really like the Concert of Nations-esque vibe of the Promise of 1528, but I agree it would've been way better if in fact it was much better determined. <br /> Much of Vampire canon is like that, specially when it comes to politics, which makes things pretty stupid, since V1. I mean, a sect having only some 7 vague laws as basis for everything is already a longshot (but it wasn't a problem cuz everything was Interview with a Vampire in scale).<br /> <br /> My vision of what happens in V5 when the Promise ends is very simple. The Hecata are getting stronger, Camarilla is getting weaker, the Hecata will (either in open war or cold war approach) takedown the sect as vengeance, they've already culled the Giovanni, now is time for the world police to suffer their wrath, since Cappadocius is a goner and their sons can't have vengeance on him. To me, if the Hecata ally even a little with the Anarchs or remnant Sabbat, they are very able to put the Camarilla on the ground.<br /> Using wraiths as proxies, they can even make the Second Inquisition work for them. <br /> <br /> I agree and like the idea of the 500 years being a probatory period at least in excuse for the armistice. To me, the Camarilla planned to bully the Giovanni Clan and take its lunch money during all that time and then erase them with the spiel that they failed in the test, and weren't exempt from their Anarch War crimes. But... things didn't go according to plan, and the Sabbat and humans proved to be way worst a problem, so Cam got its hands full.<br /> <br /> Either way, I'll be running a Chronicle with my Giovanni Chronicles group that goes through the final negotiations and signing of the Promise in Venice 1528, as part of de Corazon's retinue. They might be able to make it weight more to one sect than another, or screw them both (there are some Sabbat infiltrated members). So I've been on the lookout for every thread on the Promise for some years now. Thanks for it people","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T00:40:40-07:00","id":1536948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RadioFreeDeath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533133-the-promise-of-1528#post1533133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cult of the Blood Gods has a lore sheet for the promise of 1528 between the Giovanni and the Cam. With it coming due in less than four years it seems ripe for an entire campaign.<br /> <br /> It indicates that both sides are currently scrambling to figure out the details of the agreement so they can deal with the consequences.<br /> <br /> Where might players search to find the details of the promise? What promises would create interesting plotlines?<br /> Are the rest of the Hecata going to play ball with a promise made by only a subset?<br /> Will the Cam try to wrest Venice from the Hecata?<br /> <br /> Help me brainstorm ideas!<br /> \u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>This whole concept never made sense, like the Tremere. Both &quot;Clans&quot; should have been easily exterminated in their infancy. But &quot;Plot Armor...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T12:06:44-07:00","id":1537012,"title":"","content":"The Kindred are always out for themselves and only play lip service to honor and loyalty and weren't to broken up if clans that they viewed as disgusting or seemingly selfless got knocked down a peg.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}